    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d371">

                <pb facs="0416" n="404" sameAs="frus:frus1943v05/pg404"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.8830/2140: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Armour</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-01-14T22:00:00-04:00">January 14, 1943—10
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>68. If the Embassy perceives no objection it will please transmit to <hi
                        rendition="#italic">El Mundo</hi> the following message from the Under
                    Secretary which is in reply to one received by him from that newspaper.<anchor
                        n="57" xml:id="d371-f1"/></p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“You may be assured that this Government is making every effort to maintain
                        supplies of newsprint to <hi rendition="#italic">El Mundo</hi> as well as
                        other Argentine newspapers, and I have accordingly requested the Embassy to
                        make available to you certain details regarding these efforts.”</p>
                </quote>
                <p>The details are as follows: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>The Embassy is fully informed concerning the necessity that importer
                            make arrangements with La Flota<anchor n="58" xml:id="d371-f2"/> and
                                Dodero<anchor n="59" xml:id="d371-f3"/> in Buenos Aires to instruct
                            their agents in the United States to accept newsprint shipments.</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>The Canadian Shipping Priority Committee has appointed Mr. Irving
                            Baldwin to act as Coordinator of Shipping in New York. This assists in
                            obtaining actual shipping space for all users of Canadian newsprint.
                                (<hi rendition="#italic">La Prensa</hi> not using Canadian newsprint
                            is not included.) The Department has requested Mr. Baldwin to do
                            everything compatible with his position to give special consideration to
                                <hi rendition="#italic">El Mundo</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Critica</hi>.</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item>1000 tons of newsprint consigned to <hi rendition="#italic">El
                                Mundo</hi> will arrive in February on the following steamers: <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Rìo Salado, Rìo Gallagos, Rìo Gualeyuay</hi> and
                            SS <hi rendition="#italic">Buenos Aires</hi>.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <p>The Department is following carefully the recommendations of the Embassy as
                    indicated in despatch 1523 of November 23, 1942<anchor n="60" xml:id="d371-f4"/>
                    with respect to monthly allocations of newsprint to the consumers mentioned.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
